# The low-latency kernel.
#
# linux-lowlatency-hwe-24.04 is the 24.04 LTS hardware-enablement track of the
# lowlatency flavour: 1000 Hz tick, full preemption, and threaded interrupt
# handlers. As of this writing it carries kernel 7.0, so choosing the LTS base
# does not mean choosing an old kernel.
#
# Worth knowing before upgrading the base: Ubuntu 26.04 retires the separate
# linux-lowlatency binary package. The generic kernel there gained boot-time
# responsiveness tuning, and the flavour is replaced by linux-generic plus a
# lowlatency-kernel package that sets the GRUB command line. provision/steps/
# 20-kernel.sh knows about both and picks by release, so the base can move
# without this file changing meaning.
linux-lowlatency-hwe-24.04

# Firmware for whatever USB and network hardware the box turns out to have.
linux-firmware
